mehawk@agora.rain.com (Michael Sandy) writes:

>This has probably been discussed before, but which monsters give
>which immunities?  I had a character with a spellbook of Create
>Monster and want to know what to summon.

>Unicorns of opposite alignment make _great_ sacrifices!  If
>you change your alignment to match an altar by sacrificing, in
>almost no time you can make yourself pious in your new alignment!

>tengu give teleport control
>leprachaun teleport
>Quantum Mechs speed,

Quantum Mechanics only give speed if you are slow.    If you already are
fast, they slow you down. 

>what do nymph do?

Nymphs will give teleportation and teleport control, if you scarf down
enough of them.  Just make sure you have a good enough weapon to kill
them before they steal you blind.

  Brown pudding will give you poison resistance.
  Dragons:
    black -- disintegration resistance
    blue -- shock resistance
    orange -- sleep resistance
  Elves, also sleep resistance
  Red naga, fire ants, hell hounds and their pups, heat resistance
  Ice troll, frost wolves, blue jelly, cold resistance
  
That's all I can think of off-hand.  I make it a point to eat monsters
regularly, but it's not altogether safe before you're poison resistant. 
Stay away from yellow and violet molds unless you like to hallucinate.



